      "widgets_values": [
        "{\"version\":1,\"content\":\"<h1>KREA 2 LoRA CONVERTER</h1><p>\\n\\n</p><p>Convert a <strong>fal.ai Krea 2 LoRA</strong> into a standard LoRA that can be loaded correctly in ComfyUI.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><blockquote>\\n  LoRAs produced by the fal.ai Krea 2 trainer use layer names that ComfyUI does not recognize. This node renames those layers and saves a compatible copy without changing the trained weights.\\n</blockquote><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"LORA\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Required LoRA</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>This converter is intended for LoRAs created with the <strong>fal.ai Krea 2 Trainer</strong>.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n  <span class=\\\"pix-note-btnblock\\\">\\n    <a class=\\\"pix-note-vp\\\" style=\\\"background-color: #f66744\\\" href=\\\"https://fal.ai/models/fal-ai/krea-2-trainer\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Open fal.ai Krea 2 Trainer</a>\\n  </span>&nbsp;\\n</p><p>\\n\\n</p><div class=\\\"pix-note-folderhint\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\">Place in: ComfyUI/models/loras/krea2</div><p>\\n\\n</p><p>After adding the downloaded LoRA, refresh the model list or restart ComfyUI so the file appears in the converter dropdown.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"gear\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;How to Convert</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><ol>\\n  <li>Select the original fal.ai Krea 2 LoRA from the first dropdown.</li>\\n  <li>Review or edit the output filename.</li>\\n  <li>Leave <strong>Overwrite</strong> disabled unless you want to replace an existing converted file.</li>\\n  <li>Check the status message to confirm that the selected file is recognized as a Krea 2 LoRA.</li>\\n  <li>Click <strong>Convert</strong>.</li>\\n</ol><p>\\n\\n</p><p>The converted file is saved inside your ComfyUI LoRA folder and becomes available to normal LoRA loader nodes.</p><p>\\n\\n</p><hr class=\\\"pix-note-hr-solid\\\" style=\\\"color: #b8b8b8\\\"><p>\\n\\n</p><h2><span data-ic=\\\"pixaroma\\\" class=\\\"pix-note-ic\\\" contenteditable=\\\"false\\\" style=\\\"color: #f66744\\\"></span>&nbsp;Resources</h2><p>\\n\\n</p><p>\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-discord\\\" href=\\\"https://discord.com/invite/gggpkVgBf3\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Join Discord</a>&nbsp;\\n  <a class=\\\"pix-note-yt\\\" href=\\\"https://www.youtube.com/@pixaroma\\\" target=\\\"_blank\\\" rel=\\\"noopener noreferrer\\\">Pixaroma YouTube Channel</a>&nbsp;\\n</p>\",\"buttonColor\":\"#f66744\",\"lineColor\":\"#f66744\",\"width\":526,\"height\":975.1308540543554,\"backgroundColor\":\"#2a2a2a\"}",
